booklet and scroll down to section

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.910
three, you can see that this is
Understand the Use of Firewalls.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.140
So there's four learning objectives, and
there are four questions to allow you

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.120
to fulfill those learning objectives.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:20.910
So question one is quite straightforward.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.090
It's asking you to define
the term firewall, so what is

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.500
the definition of a firewall?

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:31.750
Again, try and put it in your own
words rather than just copying

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:35.489
the definition from the course
materials or an external site.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.879
And then for question two,
it's asked you to describe the

00:00:38.879 --> 00:00:40.470
key functions of a firewall.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.389
So what is the purpose of a firewall?

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.250
What does it do?

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.390
I would suggest for this one is to
look back at the course materials and

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:52.050
think about the different types of
firewalls and how they are applied.

00:00:52.529 --> 00:00:54.390
Do you have a firewall on your computer?

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:55.980
What is the purpose?

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.050
Have you done anything with it?

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:01.170
Did you install a firewall or is it
just already a part of your system?

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.989
So again, what is the
function of the firewall?

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:07.380
And you can personalise the
answer by explaining what the

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:08.829
firewall does for your PC.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:15.399
For question three, it's asking you define
what is meant by network traffic, so what

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:17.100
is the definition of network traffic?

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:23.949
What is the straightforward definition
of network traffic that's going across

00:01:23.949 --> 00:01:25.789
a network from computer to computer?

00:01:28.545 --> 00:01:33.225
And for question four, it's asked you to
explain the advantages and disadvantage of

00:01:33.225 --> 00:01:35.475
using a firewall to protect from threats.

00:01:35.865 --> 00:01:39.075
So think about the various
advantages and disadvantages.

00:01:39.914 --> 00:01:42.525
A lot of them are mentioned on the
course materials, but you may also

00:01:42.525 --> 00:01:47.205
have experience of advantages and
disadvantages from your own experience

00:01:47.385 --> 00:01:50.385
of using a firewall, whether it
be at work or whether it be on

00:01:50.385 --> 00:01:52.755
your home PC or your home network.

00:01:53.175 --> 00:01:55.935
So again, explain the
advantages and disadvantage.

00:01:55.935 --> 00:01:59.025
So you must give two advantages
and two disadvantages.

00:02:00.105 --> 00:02:04.455
So once you've done that, I would
recommend reading through all of the

00:02:04.605 --> 00:02:08.205
